    "title": "OpenAI expands Daybreak cybersecurity initiative with autonomous hacking capabilities",
    "summary": "On August 10, 2026, OpenAI expanded its Daybreak cybersecurity initiative with multiple new components. The company launched GPT-5.6-Cyber, a specialized cybersecurity-specific AI model designed to help security researchers and defenders identify software vulnerabilities. GPT-5.6-Cyber features fewer guardrails than standard OpenAI models, with reduced safety restrictions specifically intended for authorized vulnerability research and trusted security researchers. OpenAI introduced a two-tiered access system for Daybreak: Daybreak Blue for general defenders and Daybreak Red for authorized vulnerability researchers conducting security testing. The expansion included partnerships with 16 major cybersecurity vendors. This expansion came days after OpenAI delayed the release of its Astra model following tests that suggested it may have reached critical cybersecurity risk thresholds. The timing reflected broader industry concerns about AI agents demonstrating autonomous hacking capabilities, with multiple recent incidents of AI-powered cyber attacks documented by security researchers at conferences like Black Hat. The initiative positions defenders to use AI capabilities for identifying vulnerabilities before attackers can exploit them.",
